From 1e917ac9ae039da81abad8602c17a9cbf7effad3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: albanread <albanread@googlemail.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 11:01:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Midi Kit: the file player starts on time and stops at once

Two things made BMidiSynthFile play a song wrong, both seen in the
Midi Kit test (midikit_check) as a Stop() or delete that took 10 s:

- BMidi::Stop() sent "all notes off" and only then told the run thread
  to stop. The thread went on spraying the song between those 16
  messages, each note waited for until it was due, so Stop() took as
  long as 16 notes of the song, and the notes sent after the last "all
  notes off" went on sounding. The run thread is stopped first now.

- The soft synth loads its soundfont when first needed, and
  BMidiSynthFile::LoadFile() asked for the song's instruments through
  LoadInstrument(), which the soft synth does not implement (it printed
  UNIMPLEMENTED for each). So the soundfont was loaded at the first
  note, from the input's thread: the song was held up for as long as
  that took -- seconds on a slow disk -- and the notes due meanwhile
  then played all at once. LoadFile() loads it (LoadAllInstruments()).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Prose-Patch: 0051-midi-kit-the-file-player-starts-on-time-and-stops-at-once.patch 0c20979b92d496520fa7cfe71174bc2defc3387b4ac09568b0519232b065d4fa
---
 src/kits/midi/Midi.cpp          |  5 ++++-
 src/kits/midi/MidiSynthFile.cpp | 10 +++++-----
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/kits/midi/Midi.cpp b/src/kits/midi/Midi.cpp
index 2f957001c0..9c7108929c 100644
--- a/src/kits/midi/Midi.cpp
+++ b/src/kits/midi/Midi.cpp
@@ -211,8 +211,11 @@ BMidi::Start()
 void 
 BMidi::Stop()
 {
-	AllNotesOff();
+	// The run thread first: it would go on spraying the song between the
+	// "all notes off" messages, each note waited for until it is due, and
+	// leave the notes it sent after them sounding.
 	fThreadId = -1;
+	AllNotesOff();
 }
     
 
diff --git a/src/kits/midi/MidiSynthFile.cpp b/src/kits/midi/MidiSynthFile.cpp
index 43e961d790..306feec7a1 100644
--- a/src/kits/midi/MidiSynthFile.cpp
+++ b/src/kits/midi/MidiSynthFile.cpp
@@ -44,11 +44,11 @@ BMidiSynthFile::LoadFile(const entry_ref* midi_entry_ref)
 	status_t err = fStore->Import(midi_entry_ref);
 
 	if (err == B_OK) {
-		for (int t = 0; t < 128; ++t) {
-			if (fStore->fInstruments[t]) {
-				be_synth->fSynth->LoadInstrument(t);
-			}
-		}
+		// The soft synth has all instruments in one soundfont: load it now.
+		// Loaded at the first note instead, from the input's thread, it held
+		// up the song for as long as that took, and the notes due meanwhile
+		// then played all at once.
+		be_synth->fSynth->LoadAllInstruments();
 	}
 	
 	return err;
